      "title": "Dry run can write through copied symlinks into real directories",
      "description": "`verbatimSymlinks: true` preserves symlinks when copying install paths into the sandbox. The installer then operates on those paths in the sandbox, but filesystem operations follow the preserved links. If an install directory or file in the project points outside the sandbox, a dry run can modify or delete files at the symlink\u2019s destination, contradicting the guarantee that the project is never touched. Ensure dry-run operations cannot follow links back to real locations\u2014for example, reject or safely dereference symlinks when constructing the sandbox.",
